<Project>

  <!-- ===========================================================================================
       SECURITY (A06 - Vulnerable and Outdated Components) - solution-wide risk-acceptance record.

       AutoMapper 14.0.0 is referenced directly by WebVella.Erp and TRANSITIVELY by every project
       that depends on it (all Site hosts, all Plugins, Web, WASM Server, ConsoleApp). It carries
       HIGH advisory GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x / CVE-2026-32933 (CWE-674 Uncontrolled Recursion): a deeply
       nested or self-referential object graph pushed through a mapping path can exhaust the stack
       (StackOverflowException, i.e. denial of service).

       The upgrade is infeasible within the Minimal Change Clause:
         * The fix (a default MaxDepth of 64) ships ONLY in AutoMapper 15.1.1+/16.1.1+, which are
           RE-LICENSED from MIT to RPL-1.5 (reciprocal/copyleft) or commercial and are therefore
           incompatible with this project's Apache-2.0 license. AAP 0.3.2/0.4.2 forbid third-party
           dependency-version and license changes; 0.8.2 forbids architectural changes such as
           swapping the mapper for a non-Critical finding (this advisory is HIGH, not Critical).
         * The maintainer confirmed NO patch will be released for the 14.x (MIT) line.
         * WebVella maps only its own bounded, non-cyclic internal metadata types (Entity, Field,
           Relation, Job, User, Role, and similar); no attacker-controlled recursive object graph
           reaches an AutoMapper conversion path, so real-world exploitability is effectively absent.

       This NuGetAuditSuppress records the accepted risk for the NuGet build audit across ALL
       projects (without it, each transitive consumer re-emits NU1903 during restore and build).
       The full finding rationale is documented at WebVella.Erp/WebVella.Erp.csproj (the pinned
       direct reference) and in SECURITY.md (finding H1). Recommended long-term remediation: migrate
       to a maintained MIT-licensed mapper such as Mapperly.

       NOTE: the NuGet vulnerability listing (dotnet list package, vulnerable flag) is a
       VERSION-based query and will still list this advisory regardless of this suppression; that
       residual is documented as a risk-accepted HIGH in SECURITY.md.
       =========================================================================================== -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
